WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.330
Look, I'm not here to tell you that one decision
may be good for everybody.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.990
For instance, for some, college is good.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:11.519
You know, it works for them, so for some,
it's military, intern, backpacking and traveling,

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:16.090
but today, I'm going to make a case to you
on why this may be an option.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.789
I'm going to explain to three different audiences.

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:23.229
One is a 13, 14-year-old kid who doesn't really
know what they want to do.

00:00:23.229 --> 00:00:24.810
They've always thought, "Maybe military."

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.589
I'm going to give you some points on why you're
going to have a lot of benefits of joining

00:00:28.589 --> 00:00:29.589
military.

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:33.820
The other one's going to be an 18-year-old
kid now, becoming an adult.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.039
You're graduating high school.

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:36.059
You already did.

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:39.020
You're looking at possibly military, and it's
the parent.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.120
Some of the parents are worried about their
kids joining the military.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.989
I'll make the case to all three, and then,
you make the decision at the end what you

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:47.800
want to do because for me, I will never forget.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.640
I was 14 years old the first time I thought
about military because a guy named [Jesus

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.340
Guerrera 00:00:50] came up to me in Glendale.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.429
He said, "Hey, you want to consider joining
the military?"

00:00:57.429 --> 00:00:58.429
I got some options.

00:00:58.429 --> 00:00:59.429
I laughed at him.

00:00:59.429 --> 00:01:00.520
I said, "I'll never join the army."

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.949
Four years later, I went to him, and he recruited
me.

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:06.720
You never know the story, but I hope this
makes an impact on the way you look at military.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.200
Okay, so by the way, if you haven't yet subscribed
to the channel, please do so.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.960
If you got any comments, thoughts, questions
throughout the entire episode, comment on

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:14.960
the bottom.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.590
Number one reason why I think joining the
military will give you benefits that you will

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:24.399
not have in college is classroom-style teaching
versus real life.

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:27.930
In college, it's a lot of classroom.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.890
Somebody talks from up there, and you sit
down.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.290
You take notes.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:36.770
You're learning to your best abilities, but
we know the best way we learn is hands-on.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.510
It's somebody working there with me.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.950
It's somebody showing me, "Here's how you
do it.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.521
Look how I do it, and then, you do it.

00:01:43.521 --> 00:01:44.521
Look how I do it.

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:45.950
Then, you do it."

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.200
My kids go to a private school.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.100
Yesterday, we had a parent ... What do you
call this?

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.509
A parent-teacher conference type of thing.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:52.630
I went to it last night.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.159
One of the things they believe in, which is
the reason why I like this school is they

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:01.850
believe kids learn more by playing, by building,
by doing instead of lecturing.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.060
I think college, sometimes, it's way too much
lecturing.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.570
There isn't somebody getting there and showing
to them how to do it.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:11.651
Now, if there is a college you're going to
that does do that, more power to them, but

00:02:11.651 --> 00:02:14.080
most colleges, it's more classroom style.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.930
Number two, problem solving on the go.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.790
I don't know if you learn problem solving
on the go in college.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.850
I do know you're going to learn it in the
military all the time.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:27.600
I mean I can't tell you how many times we'd
be in the back 40 or we're working in the

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.120
fields.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.881
Something would come up, and you don't have
a long time to be thinking about it.

00:02:31.881 --> 00:02:33.640
You got to figure out a way to solve it right
there.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.220
"Hey, [John 00:02:34], what are we going to
do?"

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.220
"Let's do this."

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.220
"Okay, great.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.220
Give me that.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.220
Give me.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.220
Let's grab this."

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.200
You have to go on the go, so it created your
brain to be able to constantly think about

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.470
problem solving on the go.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.320
By the way, one of the things that you'll
realize value to, and I talk about one subject

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.640
mainly, which is entrepreneurship.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.650
Everything is around entrepreneurship.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.840
You will see a lot of these things that you
learn in the military will help somebody who

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.450
wants to one day run a business.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.000
Number three, teamwork.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.750
They don't teach you teamwork in college.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.570
Honestly, think about it.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.700
They do not teach you teamwork in college.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.810
Maybe a couple group projects you do, but
there's not really emphasis on teamwork.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:17.590
Do you realize, I would tell you everything
we did in the military was all teamwork.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:23.550
Everything we did from bootcamp to AIT to
being at the 101st Airborne Division Air Assault

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:29.720
to breakfast, to running, to exercising to
working to projects.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.360
Everything was teamwork.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.780
Everything was you have a buddy.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.370
Everything was you have somebody.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.300
You got to have their back to have your back.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.920
Everything they taught you was about teamwork.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:47.960
One of the things I will tell you that's the
toughest things any CEO, leader, parent, coach,

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:53.870
the toughest thing anyone struggles with is
to create an environment where everybody is

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.500
working together as a team.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.320
I've been running a business for a long time.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.950
I'm going to tell you something here.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.611
One of the things I miss from the military
when I got out was the comradery of how it

00:04:02.611 --> 00:04:03.611
was to build a team.

00:04:03.611 --> 00:04:08.560
I told myself, whatever I do, wherever I work,
I'm always going to bring that tool.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.840
When I worked at Bally's, it was absolute
teamwork.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.550
When we kicked every other gym's butt, it
was teamwork.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.900
When I went into sales, it was teamwork.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.370
When I was running a company, it was teamwork.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.310
When it's running a family, team.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.729
Everything to me is stemmed from teamwork.

00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:27.229
College is too much about you, you, you, you,
you.

00:04:27.229 --> 00:04:28.229
Military was about team.

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:29.229
We can do something big together.

00:04:29.229 --> 00:04:30.900
Number four, diversity.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.330
I'm from Iran, okay?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.990
I joined the military, and I go to a bootcamp.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:43.060
I'm in South Carolina, and there's people
there from South Dakota, North Dakota, Mississippi.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.350
You got Arkansas.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.169
You got people from Oklahoma, people from
Montana.

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:51.039
They have never met a Middle-Eastern before,
right?

00:04:51.039 --> 00:04:57.020
I didn't know anybody from New York or Miami
or Chicago or all these other places.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:03.189
You hang out together, and you learn about
different diversity, and you learn about cultures.

00:05:03.189 --> 00:05:04.600
You learn about certain communities.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:09.150
You learn about what's important to them,
and what's important to ... You learn so much

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:14.419
about diversity that, yes, you may pick up
in college because may make the case and say,

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:17.170
"Well, in college, people go to college from
all across the country as well."

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.039
In many cases, from all over the world.

00:05:19.039 --> 00:05:21.009
I get it, but you're in the classroom.

00:05:21.009 --> 00:05:22.360
You don't have to do anything with them.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.620
You're just in a classroom.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.069
In the military, you have to work with them.

00:05:26.069 --> 00:05:28.759
You have to get to know them because it's
teamwork.

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:32.139
I have to get to know who you are because
I'm going to work on this project with you

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:33.139
for three weeks.

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:34.319
I have to know you.

00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:35.930
I don't have to know you in college.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:39.139
I may party with you, but I don't have to
know you.

00:05:39.139 --> 00:05:40.689
We're just in a classroom together.

00:05:40.689 --> 00:05:43.550
Number five, independence.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.590
Smallest listing, watch this.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:49.310
The smallest thing is you have to wash your
own clothes.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.169
You have to iron your clothes.

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:57.830
You have to learn about starch and crease
and shining your shoes and making sure your

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.949
room is clean, right?

00:05:59.949 --> 00:06:01.750
You got to mop the floor.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:06.050
When's the last time a teenager mopped the
floor seven days a week?

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.819
You got to learn how to clean.

00:06:08.819 --> 00:06:13.199
You'll learn a lot of the independent stuff
that you have to make decisions on your own.

00:06:13.199 --> 00:06:15.139
You got to make decisions.

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:16.139
It's on you now.

00:06:16.139 --> 00:06:18.190
There is no more hiding behind mommy and daddy.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:22.979
Some of the parents that are afraid of having
their kids join the military at the same like,

00:06:22.979 --> 00:06:25.219
"I want my kids to also be independent."

00:06:25.219 --> 00:06:26.219
Yes, but you know?

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:28.490
A little bit of this that makes a lot of sense,
right?

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:29.699
You learn a lot about those.

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:33.159
By the way, sometimes, a teenager was like,
"Get off my back.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:35.529
Let me make my own decisions a little bit
for myself."

00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:37.990
The military may not be a bad option for you.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.960
Number six, mental and emotional toughness.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.919
Honestly, if you ask me, I was asking [Jessica
00:06:42] earlier.

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:46.749
I said, "What is the opposite of a softie?"

00:06:46.749 --> 00:06:48.590
You know, somebody who is a softie.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.479
I see a lot of people that are soft.

00:06:51.479 --> 00:06:54.180
I see a lot of people that are too sensitive.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.479
I see a lot of people that are too emotional.

00:06:56.479 --> 00:06:58.809
I see a lot of people that are not too stable.

00:06:58.809 --> 00:07:00.069
I just see a lot of that.

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:03.620
By the way, I'm not just talking about millennials,
Gen X's.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.699
This is a young generation thing, not at all.

00:07:05.699 --> 00:07:07.650
I was a softie.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.099
Completely in high school, I was a softie.

00:07:10.099 --> 00:07:14.009
The military toughened me up mentally and
emotionally.

00:07:14.009 --> 00:07:15.949
I learned what it is to be mentally tough.

00:07:15.949 --> 00:07:17.740
I learned what it is to be emotionally tough.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:22.360
By the way, there's a part of it that you
may go into bootcamp and realize you can't

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.979
hack it, and you get out.

00:07:24.979 --> 00:07:28.199
There's a part of you when you go in, and
you realize you can do a lot more than you

00:07:28.199 --> 00:07:29.559
thought you could do.

00:07:29.559 --> 00:07:33.220
By the way, in the business world, if you
are not mentally and emotionally tough, the

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.169
business world definitely ain't for you.

00:07:35.169 --> 00:07:38.840
This could be a good wake-up call into one
day running your own business.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:39.970
I got a message yesterday.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:40.970
What was it?

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:41.970
Guy on Snapchat.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.139
What was he, marines?

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:44.139
He's in marines.

00:07:44.139 --> 00:07:45.990
He watches every single Valuetainment video.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.259
He says, "I'm in the marines right now."

00:07:48.259 --> 00:07:49.400
He shows me his entire barracks.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.059
He says, "I watch every single Valuetainment
video because I cannot wait to get out of

00:07:54.059 --> 00:07:56.539
the marines so I can become an entrepreneur."

00:07:56.539 --> 00:08:00.440
Well, good for him, because he's also got
the mental and the emotional toughness from

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.689
being in the marines.

00:08:01.689 --> 00:08:04.050
Number seven, hands-on leadership.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.630
Let me tell you about hands-on leadership.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.650
Oh my gosh.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.520
Someone's working with you constantly.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:14.740
I talked about it briefly about real life
style, but you have somebody's always hands-on

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:15.740
with you.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.370
There's a certain level of accountability.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.190
I would put seven and eight together.

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:20.659
This is why I have it like this.

00:08:20.659 --> 00:08:24.330
Number eight, hands-on leadership demands
discipline.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.340
You got to be disciplined.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.909
Let me explain.

00:08:26.909 --> 00:08:29.960
First time I went to college, and I went into
my classroom.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.539
It was me and this other guy named [Armand
00:08:31].

00:08:31.539 --> 00:08:36.180
By the way, he runs a business that does 12
million dollars a year, very successful guy.

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.520
We got our class, and the professor's name
is [Van Dam 00:08:38], okay?

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.020
What a great name, by the way, English teacher,
Van Dam.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:48.090
We go into this class, and he says, "Hey,
I just want you guys to know this.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.580
You're officially adults.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.030
If you don't want to be in my classroom, you
don't have to be in my classroom.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.970
There are no roll calls to all the freshmen
here.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.770
You don't have to" ... He went through this
whole thing.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.850
I looked at him, and I'm like, "You got to
be kidding me.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.850
These guys are serious.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.680
I thought they were kidding that you don't
have to be in a classroom."

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.310
No, you don't have to be in a classroom.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.620
I said, "Bro, let's get out of here."

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.620
We got up.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:08.620
We went outside.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.620
We sat in front of the cafeteria.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.950
We played spades every single day.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.430
We never went to Mr. Van Dam's classroom.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.110
A girl there would tell us what the homework
was.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:19.470
We would do our best, and that was it, but
we went to play spades.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:22.360
We would play spades because there is no accountability.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.320
That teacher doesn't care if you come to the
classroom or not.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.800
In a military, you have to come to the classroom.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.530
I mean what do you mean you're not coming
to training?

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:30.700
You're going to get an Article 15.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:37.040
You have certain responsibilities and accountability,
which in some ways, this teaches that to become

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.210
a habit because you always show up.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:42.880
Sometimes, this game of life is just about
showing up.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:47.220
Sometimes, college tells you, you don't have
to show up if you don't want to show up.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.910
Military shows you, you got to show up.

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:50.460
Number nine, seeing the world.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.330
You're going to travel and see the world.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:55.800
I can tell you for myself, when people ask
me questions, and they say about how much

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.470
fun I had, man, I had a lot of fun in the
army.

00:09:58.470 --> 00:09:59.470
I mean really.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.940
I had a lot of fun in the army.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:06.370
I am always grateful that Instagram wasn't
around when I was in the army.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:12.300
You have no idea how grateful I am that Instagram
came out after my partying days because it

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:13.300
would be embarrassing.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:19.760
Some of the short clips and pictures you would
see about my army days on how hard we partied

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.680
in the army when we saw the world.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.740
You're going to see the world.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:23.740
You're going to have a good time.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:24.880
Number 10, respect.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:27.580
You'll learn respect for elders.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.510
You'll learn respect for the game.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:30.650
You'll learn respect.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.490
It teaches respect for the opponent.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.030
It teaches respect for the enemy.

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:37.930
It teaches respect for your competition because
you always have to be prepared if an enemy

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.670
decides to attack you.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:43.000
There's respect for a lot of different things,
right, that you'll learn, but they teach you

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.210
that in the military.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.410
Number 11, constantly being challenged.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.020
You're always going to be pushed.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:49.020
I don't care what it is.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.460
There isn't a single minute that you're not
being pushed.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.460
You're always being challenged to improve.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.390
Number 12, you stay in shape.

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:57.780
You want to be successful in life, you got
to have energy, enthusiasm.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:58.930
You got to have stamina.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:02.851
If you don't have the energy, you don't stay
in shape, you're just not going to cut it

00:11:02.851 --> 00:11:05.540
in the world of business because you're going
to last a long time.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:10.080
In the world of military, every day, you have
to exercise when you're in the military.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.120
Number 13, lesser chances of doing drugs.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.790
Now, don't get me wrong here.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.350
You're going to see drugs.

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:17.730
I saw a lot of drugs.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:21.300
One that I'm doing guard duty, and I'm going
to one of my guys' rooms.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.740
He had a mountain of nose candy on his table.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.060
You know what nose candy is.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.080
It's cocaine, right?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.600
He had a mountain of cocaine.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:30.250
I'm like ... I don't want to say his name.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.120
I said, "Brother, you cannot be doing all
this cocaine."

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.430
He says, "Well, a guy named [Rob 00:11:33]
gave it to me."

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.890
I even knew this other guy.

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:38.300
I said, "I get it, but you can't do it.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.300
You're going to go to jail."

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.410
A month later, he gets caught.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.730
He goes to military prison.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.300
It's not the way to do it.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.470
Everybody saw, if you do cocaine in the military,
you're going to go to prison.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:53.160
You definitely don't want to go in the military
prison, right?

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.311
There's a lot of accountability that if you
did any of that stuff, you lose it.

00:11:56.311 --> 00:11:57.480
You lose your rank.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.480
You lose everything.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.490
In college, if you smoke pot, do you lose
a class?

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.300
Do you go from sophomore to a freshman?

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.300
No.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.300
There is no accountability.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.300
No one cares if you do drugs.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.810
As a matter of fact, you know, a lot of people
do drugs in college.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:11.120
Military, if you do, there is consequences.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:14.640
You work your butt off to become an E-5 or
an E-6 or an E-4.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:15.640
You screw up.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:16.640
You're going to go back down.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:22.280
That fear of losing that, people protect themselves
from not doing the drug part.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.280
Number 14, benefits.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.190
You got a lot of benefits.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.190
Listen.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:27.860
Benefits is one, healthcare.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:28.860
I'll blow it right now.

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:32.060
They don't have the best benefits that they
take care with the VAs, but I'm going to tell

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.740
you benefits on a different side.

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:37.280
When I say benefits, this is what I mean.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:43.880
I got hired at Morgan Stanley Dean Witter
at 21 years old when I got my series seven,

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:49.630
and I became a broker, I got hired because
the guy who hired me, a man named [Dave Kurby

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:54.630
00:12:48] liked the fact that I had a military
background.

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:55.630
That's why he hired me.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:56.630
He saw my resume.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.080
He said, "Do you have any college experience?"

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.080
I say, "A little bit.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:00.080
I went to Sta.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:03.670
Monica Community College and Glendale Community
College, but that's all I got."

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.140
He says, "Do you have a four-year or two-year?"

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.140
I don't.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.850
It was me and another girl who graduated in
Berkeley.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.780
She did a four-year program in two and a half
years.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:10.780
Genius girl.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.400
He says, "But you were in the military, right?

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.590
They teach you discipline and hard work in
the military."

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:15.590
"Yes."

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:16.590
"I like that.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:17.590
You have the job as well."

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:18.590
Both of us were hired.

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:19.590
She was college.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:20.590
I was military.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:21.590
We both were hired.

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:24.270
The benefits on the resume being in the military
helps you to do a lot of other things in your

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.270
career.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:30.370
I like when I'm hiring somebody if they have
military background, I know their skin is

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:31.370
thick.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.780
They're not soft.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:33.780
They're not weak.

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.660
They're willing to work hard they're disciplined.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.040
They know what it is to work like a team.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.830
I know that, so I like that on resumes.

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:40.830
I like working.

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:45.410
Matter of fact, the top earners that I work
with, the best sales people in our company,

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.090
he has military experience.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.440
He was in the marines for eight years.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:51.230
He did three tours in Afghanistan and all
these other places.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.230
He's tough.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.720
He's great at bringing everybody together.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:54.850
I like that part, right?

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:58.350
I don't have to call this person, not knowing
if he's going to get sensitive, upset at me

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.850
because he comes from that world.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:01.960
Then, you have college paid for.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:03.440
It's crazy.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:09.300
If you go to college, you don't necessarily
learn disciple, but if you go to military,

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.220
you can go to college at the same time.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.800
There was a lot of guys that were in the unit
with me.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.910
You know, military endorses you to go to college.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.110
They want you to go to college.

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:19.090
They don't mind if you have classrooms that
night.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:22.190
There was a lot of guys that got their four-year
degrees when they were in there for four years

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:26.400
as well at the same time, so you can get your
Bachelor's when you're in there.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:30.140
Get all these other benefits and still get
your college degree while you're in the military.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.870
They're going to give you scholarships for
that as well.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.350
Last but not the least is the obvious one.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.740
You've got to work hard.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.120
You will definitely work hard.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:41.360
I mean I can tell you, I never thought I could
work 36 hours straight until I did.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:45.510
You're going to, without coffee, without anything,
just water.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.510
You're going to work hard.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:49.580
You're going to push that limit where you
hit.

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:53.170
When you hit that limit, you know what you
start realizing afterwards?

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:56.681
When you got to another company or wherever
you want to move up in a company, there's

00:14:56.681 --> 00:14:57.860
one things you're not afraid of.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:01.380
You are not afraid of out-working anybody
because nothing's going to be more work than

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.300
the work you did in the military.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.300
Nothing is.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.930
There's not a single job you'll ever do that
will be more work than the military.

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:13.660
It's just not going to be, not going to be,
so that will give you an edge as well in the

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.451
military of learning how to work hard.

00:15:15.451 --> 00:15:16.860
These are 16 points.

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:20.360
By the way, if somebody can come and do a
video in saying 16 reasons why you ought to

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:23.930
join the college instead of military, they
can give their arguments.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:28.280
There probably is going to be some valid arguments
there as well, but I'm just telling you right

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.280
now.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:34.200
I would say for every 20 that goes to college,
only a couple go to the military.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.020
There's a lot of benefits of getting involved
in the military.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:39.410
If you have any questions, thoughts, comments,
comment on the bottom.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:45.050
If you haven't yet subscribed to this channel,
click here to subscribe to the channel.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.110
Take care, everybody.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.140
Bye, bye.

